<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>International news from the Americas - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24’s coverage of the political, social and economic issues in the United States, Canada, Mexico, Argentina, Brazil and across the Americas.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/</link><lastBuildDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 13:22:51 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category></category><title>Former gang member found guilty of murdering rapper Tupac Shakur</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/former-gang-member-found-guilty-of-murdering-rapper-tupac-shakur</link><description>
A jury found Duane “Keffe D” Davis guilty of orchestrating the 1996 killing of rap icon Tupac Shakur, finally bringing a measure of resolution to a case that had gripped hip-hop fans and lingered in the public imagination for decades. Davis could be sentenced to life in prison following that verdict. FRANCE 24's Wassim Cornet tells us more about the verdict.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/716b80a8-9567-11f1-8f27-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/tupac-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/716b80a8-9567-11f1-8f27-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/tupac-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">08f85520-a5e1-11f1-b0fe-4312efd22778</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 09:31:34 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Government air strikes kill 20 alleged guerrillas in Colombia, president says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260901-government-air-strikes-kill-20-alleged-guerrillas-in-colombia-president-says</link><description>
Fresh government air strikes have killed 20 alleged members of the Central General Staff (EMC) armed group in southern Colombia, the country's new right-wing President Abelardo de la Espriella said Monday. The new administration carried out two other deadly air strikes against suspected guerrillas in August, which sources within Colombia's forensics authority say killed at least four minors.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2f57d844-a5c3-11f1-aeb0-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP24236497026995.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2f57d844-a5c3-11f1-aeb0-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP24236497026995.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9b44020e-a5c2-11f1-a303-0376ece26ef1</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 05:42:42 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2f57d844-a5c3-11f1-aeb0-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP24236497026995.jpg">© Fernando Vergara, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Duane 'Keffe D' Davis found guilty in Tupac Shakur murder</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260901-duane-keffe-d-davis-found-guilty-in-tupac-shakur-murder</link><description>
Duane “Keffe D” Davis was found guilty Monday of orchestrating the 1996 murder of rap icon Tupac Shakur, becoming the first person convicted in the decades-old case. The 63-year-old faces a possible life sentence after a Las Vegas jury deliberated for less than three hours.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/18f9a702-a59c-11f1-8391-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26243678304338.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/18f9a702-a59c-11f1-8391-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26243678304338.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9a6e66d0-a59f-11f1-a753-87e6ac0d77a5</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 00:53:52 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/18f9a702-a59c-11f1-8391-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26243678304338.jpg">© Steve Marcus/Pool Reuters via AP </source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Fashion designer Galliano calls off Met Gala exhibit as backlash over anti-Semitic rant mounts</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260831-fashion-designer-galliano-calls-off-met-gala-exhibit-as-backlash-over-anti-semitic-rant-mounts</link><description>
A planned nine-month retrospective of the work of fashion designer John Galliano at New York's Metropolitan Museum of Art has been called off following backlash over the British designer's 2011 conviction for anti-Semitic and anti-Asian comments. Footage surfaced in 2011 showing Galliano hurling racist and anti-Semitic slurs at patrons in a Paris bar the previous year.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7231e9ba-a56f-11f1-81ba-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/40022b4bf464b65b67794bfb36fd6f28d531a250.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7231e9ba-a56f-11f1-81ba-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/40022b4bf464b65b67794bfb36fd6f28d531a250.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7325f2d0-a56f-11f1-96f2-3db0a493d827</guid><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 19:09:10 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7231e9ba-a56f-11f1-81ba-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/40022b4bf464b65b67794bfb36fd6f28d531a250.jpg">© Kirill Kudryavtsev, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Colombian rebel group say kidnapped French Foreign Legion soldier is still alive</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260831-colombian-rebel-group-say-kidnapped-french-foreign-legion-soldier-is-still-alive</link><description>
Rebels from the Central General Staff, the main splinter group of Colombia's defunct FARC guerrillas, on Sunday said they were responsible for kidnapping a Colombian national serving in the elite French Foreign Legion. The guerrillas said that Jose Olger Melo Charry, who was reportedly on leave in his home country, was alive and in "perfect health".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e8687fb2-a4e9-11f1-afc5-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/7a73bca64d2e0376afbcfb772cc26314da71d427.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e8687fb2-a4e9-11f1-afc5-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/7a73bca64d2e0376afbcfb772cc26314da71d427.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">497b88e4-a51c-11f1-ab19-31227608711c</guid><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 09:54:28 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e8687fb2-a4e9-11f1-afc5-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/7a73bca64d2e0376afbcfb772cc26314da71d427.jpg">© Raul Arboleda, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Vance to address Republican Jewish Coalition as activists raise concerns over anti-Semitism</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260831-vance-to-address-republican-jewish-coalition-as-activists-raise-concerns-over-anti-semitism</link><description>
US Vice President JD Vance will make a private address on Monday at the annual gathering of the Republican Jewish Coalition, a collection of conservative Jewish activists. Vance's more equivocal stance on Israel has been criticised by some pro-Israel figures within the conservative movement, who have also raised concerns over his refusal to distance himself from commentators such as Tucker Carlson, who have given a platform to far-right anti-Semitic figures.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/68b35bea-a505-11f1-8a11-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26236611925842.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/68b35bea-a505-11f1-8a11-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26236611925842.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3bea24e6-a504-11f1-8a11-799f1d4fdb10</guid><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 07:05:23 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/68b35bea-a505-11f1-8a11-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26236611925842.jpg">© Anna Moneymaker, Getty Image via AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Two dead and around 15 missing as flash flood strikes Grand Canyon National Park</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260831-grand-canyon-national-park-flash-flood-missing</link><description>
At least two people died and more than 15 people may be missing after flash floods struck Grand Canyon National Park in Arizona, the National Park Service said on Sunday. Flooding hit the Bright Angel Canyon and Phantom Ranch area on Saturday, prompting authorities to evacuate visitors and search for people who remain unaccounted for.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b4ac9a16-a4bf-11f1-bc9a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26242727343846.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b4ac9a16-a4bf-11f1-bc9a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26242727343846.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">48093f1a-a4bd-11f1-9478-35ea64fe1085</guid><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 01:38:50 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b4ac9a16-a4bf-11f1-bc9a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26242727343846.jpg">© James Thompson, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>US Treasury bars certain journalists from G20 meeting in North Carolina</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260830-us-treasury-journalists-from-g20</link><description>
The US Treasury Department denied credentials to reporters from The New York Times, The Wall Street Journal and Bloomberg for a G20 finance meeting in North Carolina, the latest restriction on media access under US President Donald Trump. Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent said the decision was unrelated to journalists’ viewpoints.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/552900fe-9ff4-11f1-9dfb-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/348da3527c6d3d2c0b2149d797c9ea9560ee6767.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/552900fe-9ff4-11f1-9dfb-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/348da3527c6d3d2c0b2149d797c9ea9560ee6767.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0f4813d0-a4c3-11f1-9865-31d4a2f58c7c</guid><pubDate>Sun, 30 Aug 2026 22:48:02 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/552900fe-9ff4-11f1-9dfb-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/348da3527c6d3d2c0b2149d797c9ea9560ee6767.jpg">© Kent NISHIMURA, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Trump says NBC journalist to be reported to FCC for ‘punishment’ over endorsement coverage</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260830-trump-says-nbc-journalist-to-be-reported-to-fcc-for-punishment-over-endorsement-coverage</link><description>
US President Donald Trump on Sunday said prominent NBC anchor ​Kristen Welker will be reported to the Federal Communications Commission (FCC) for "rebuke or punishment" after she reported the Republican president had "mixed results" in his endorsement ​of candidates for the November midterm elections. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e36f8728-a492-11f1-a5ae-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26130554165647.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e36f8728-a492-11f1-a5ae-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26130554165647.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d911b3b8-a493-11f1-8876-2fc47e9ce1ee</guid><pubDate>Sun, 30 Aug 2026 17:06:53 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e36f8728-a492-11f1-a5ae-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26130554165647.jpg">© Jose Luis Magana, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US and Venezuela seal 25-year oil deal</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/us-and-venezuela-seal-25-year-oil-deal</link><description>
US President Donald Trump has called it “the biggest oil deal in world history”, while Venezuela’s interim president has assured the public that the country will retain control of its oil under the agreement. The “historic” 25-year deal with Washington involves 65 billion barrels of Venezuelan oil and aims to allow the country to develop its oil industry while preserving “ownership of and sovereignty” over its resources, Rodriguez said in a televised address. Rachael Griffiths has more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4491d1dc-a466-11f1-9433-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260830-121001-121146-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4491d1dc-a466-11f1-9433-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260830-121001-121146-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">49e481ac-a466-11f1-9dcb-6f9a81a1cdb5</guid><pubDate>Sun, 30 Aug 2026 11:34:36 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Argentines march on Peter Thiel's mansion</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/argentines-march-on-peter-thiel-s-mansion</link><description>
In Argentina, protesters marched toward a mansion reportedly purchased by American tech billionaire Peter Thiel. Activists accuse Thiel of seeking to profit from the country’s natural resources and wielding excessive political influence in the South American nation. Peter O'Brien reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/af588c0a-a456-11f1-957d-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260830-110822-111000-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/af588c0a-a456-11f1-957d-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260830-110822-111000-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b479fef8-a456-11f1-945c-57cf20512793</guid><pubDate>Sun, 30 Aug 2026 10:06:31 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>NASA launches Roman telescope to map 'a new atlas of the universe'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260830-nasa-set-to-launch-roman-telescope-to-map-the-universe</link><description>
NASA on Sunday launched its Roman Space Telescope aboard a SpaceX Falcon Heavy rocket, beginning a multi-year mission to create a vast new map of the cosmos. With a field of view far wider than Hubble’s, Roman will search for exoplanets and supernovae while also probing two of the biggest mysteries in physics: dark matter and dark energy.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/54b1beee-a432-11f1-8b6d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-29T195602Z-94810877-RC2I8NAYVGKF-RTRMADP-3-SPACE-NASA-TELESCOPE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/54b1beee-a432-11f1-8b6d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-29T195602Z-94810877-RC2I8NAYVGKF-RTRMADP-3-SPACE-NASA-TELESCOPE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c9561506-a432-11f1-a91a-574a0623f441</guid><pubDate>Sun, 30 Aug 2026 05:26:07 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/54b1beee-a432-11f1-8b6d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-29T195602Z-94810877-RC2I8NAYVGKF-RTRMADP-3-SPACE-NASA-TELESCOPE.jpg">© Joe Skipper, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>'I am sure of myself': A look back at Dolly Parton's unspoken feminist legacy</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260829-i-am-sure-of-myself-a-look-back-at-dolly-parton-s-unspoken-feminist-legacy</link><description>
Beloved country star Dolly Parton was many things to her fans, including an actor, singer, philanthropist and entrepreneur. But after her death on Tuesday at the age of 80, some admirers are remembering her as something she never overtly claimed: feminist icon.  
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/da06009a-a3b1-11f1-84a0-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP23226848721521.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/da06009a-a3b1-11f1-84a0-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP23226848721521.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">04511ff6-a3b2-11f1-b38b-77bfbb7f6ae8</guid><pubDate>Sat, 29 Aug 2026 15:57:29 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/da06009a-a3b1-11f1-84a0-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP23226848721521.jpg">© Charlie Riedel, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US to control one fifth of Venezuela's oil reserves, Trump says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/us-to-control-one-fifth-of-venezuela-s-oil-reserves-trump-says</link><description>
President Donald Trump on Friday announced an unprecedented US push ​to take control of a fifth of Venezuela's vast oil reserves, betting that American companies can revive the OPEC nation's battered energy industry while delivering a new source of crude to help bring down US fuel prices.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/30cda30c-a384-11f1-abfb-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260829-100823-100959-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/30cda30c-a384-11f1-abfb-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260829-100823-100959-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">36119aa8-a384-11f1-98b4-a176131393b9</guid><pubDate>Sat, 29 Aug 2026 08:55:18 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Trump announces 'historic' agreement for US stake in Venezuela oil reserves</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260829-trump-announces-historic-agreement-for-us-stake-in-venezuela-oil-reserves</link><description>
Washington and Caracas announced Friday that they had reached a “historic” oil agreement, under which the United States will take majority control of more than 65 billion barrels of Venezuela's reserves.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c1055f6e-a348-11f1-9143-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/edd03e0c728c7cb6cd2123619620f6487d1bda99.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c1055f6e-a348-11f1-9143-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/edd03e0c728c7cb6cd2123619620f6487d1bda99.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">51fa6eee-a33d-11f1-94f6-513b0119b9b2</guid><pubDate>Sat, 29 Aug 2026 00:05:18 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c1055f6e-a348-11f1-9143-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/edd03e0c728c7cb6cd2123619620f6487d1bda99.jpg">© Margioni Bermudez, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US-CANADA: Trump signs order renaming Lake Ontario to ‘Lake America’</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260828-us-canada-trump-signs-order-renaming-lake-ontario-to-lake-america</link><description>
US President Donald Trump signed an executive order on August 27 to rename Lake Ontario as 'Lake America', a change he said would take effect immediately. Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney took to X, writing the Great Lake's name will remain 'now and always'. The order comes after US-Canada trade talks collapsed last week, prompting the two longtime allies to announce tit-for-tat tariffs
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4eef493a-a2d0-11f1-8958-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Sequence-08-00-00-10-00-Still002.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4eef493a-a2d0-11f1-8958-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Sequence-08-00-00-10-00-Still002.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">93057ef4-a2cc-11f1-ade0-131f88726134</guid><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 12:16:51 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US : Tate brothers remain in jail as judge delays bail decision</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/us-tate-brothers-remain-in-jail-as-judge-delays-bail-decision</link><description>
Andrew and Tristan Tate will remain in custody in Miami after a federal judge declined to rule on their bail request as they fight extradition to the UK, where they face charges including rape, assault, human trafficking and money laundering. The UK has until mid-September to submit its evidence to the US State Department, while the brothers continue to deny wrongdoing and claim their online personas were fictional.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b13ff79a-a2b9-11f1-8c8c-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260828-070940-071105-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b13ff79a-a2b9-11f1-8c8c-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260828-070940-071105-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b619a0fe-a2b9-11f1-ae54-3536965512b5</guid><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 09:10:00 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>French Foreign Legion soldier kidnapped in Colombia</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260828-french-foreign-legion-soldier-kidnapped-in-colombia</link><description>
Colombian military announced Thursday that a French-Colombian soldier from the French Foreign Legion was kidnapped in early August while travelling in the department of Narino. The kidnappers are believed to be members of the Estado Mayor Central, dissidents from the far-left FARC guerrilla group.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/381c88c8-a300-11f1-8f3f-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-442J3MQ-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/381c88c8-a300-11f1-8f3f-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-442J3MQ-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">41c39afc-a29b-11f1-8dcd-f9ae98cc830c</guid><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 05:24:45 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/381c88c8-a300-11f1-8f3f-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-442J3MQ-1.jpg">© Manon Cruz, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>US military faces ‘beyond critical’ shortage of Patriot missiles in Europe</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260827-us-military-faces-beyond-critical-shortage-of-patriot-missiles-in-europe</link><description>
The US military is running critically low on Patriot missile interceptors in Europe as the war with Iran drains stocks, according to US and NATO officials. The shortfall is raising concerns about NATO’s ability to counter a potential Russian ballistic missile attack, though officials said no such assault is imminent.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9fa3d084-8d1e-11f1-aa4f-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP23037440334200.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9fa3d084-8d1e-11f1-aa4f-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP23037440334200.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">08e8bfe0-a260-11f1-9e47-774cf3c289c3</guid><pubDate>Thu, 27 Aug 2026 21:41:16 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9fa3d084-8d1e-11f1-aa4f-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP23037440334200.jpg">© Michal Dyjuk, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Trump signs order to rename Lake Ontario to 'Lake America' as Carney pushes back</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260827-trump-signs-order-to-rename-lake-ontario-to-lake-america-as-carney-pushes-back</link><description>
US President Donald Trump on Thursday signed an executive order to update the name of Lake Ontario to "Lake America" in the country's geographic naming service. Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney pushed back, citing the name's Indigenous origins, as the row between the neighbors roiled on.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f98d9008-a254-11f1-8d70-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26239645255623.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f98d9008-a254-11f1-8d70-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26239645255623.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bc177a0c-a256-11f1-abee-ab5ce4851fa7</guid><pubDate>Thu, 27 Aug 2026 20:39:59 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f98d9008-a254-11f1-8d70-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26239645255623.jpg">© Manuel Balce Ceneta, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Why Trump wants H-1B skilled worker visas to cost employers more than $100,000</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260827-why-trump-wants-h-1b-skilled-worker-visas-to-cost-employers-more-than-100-000</link><description>
US President Donald Trump is once again trying to impose a $100,000 fee on employers seeking to hire skilled temporary foreign workers through the H-1B visa programme. But while tech titans like Elon Musk have long championed the programme to draw top global talent to Silicon Valley, critics on both left and right say the scheme aims to replace skilled US-born workers with cheaper – and more easily controlled – foreign guest workers. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dae37bd4-a22e-11f1-b32d-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP17108734234193.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dae37bd4-a22e-11f1-b32d-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP17108734234193.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0237040e-a22e-11f1-80a6-6b2811ee2df9</guid><pubDate>Thu, 27 Aug 2026 17:24:55 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dae37bd4-a22e-11f1-b32d-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP17108734234193.jpg">© Susan Walsh, AP</source><dc:creator>Paul MILLAR</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Alleged 9/11 mastermind Khalid Sheikh Mohammed to go on trial in 2028</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260827-alleged-9-11-mastermind-khalid-sheikh-mohammed-to-go-on-trial-in-2028</link><description>
A spokesman for the US military court at Guantanamo Bay said Thursday that Khalid Sheikh Mohammed – the alleged mastermind of the September 11, 2001 attacks on the United States – will go on trial before a US military court in June 2028. Mohammed, also known as "KSM", was considered one of Osama bin Laden's top lieutenants before he was captured in March 2003.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0c1d8938-a21b-11f1-b25b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/f2572592d06f0f1ac1c2bfb6ac2d020c3dc3fd5e.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0c1d8938-a21b-11f1-b25b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/f2572592d06f0f1ac1c2bfb6ac2d020c3dc3fd5e.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0cce2478-a21b-11f1-87c3-f5fc7d690f61</guid><pubDate>Thu, 27 Aug 2026 13:27:28 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0c1d8938-a21b-11f1-b25b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/f2572592d06f0f1ac1c2bfb6ac2d020c3dc3fd5e.jpg">© AFP </source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>FDA approves new drug Rasonque to treat advanced pancreatic cancer</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260826-fda-approves-new-drug-rasonque-to-treat-advanced-pancreatic-cancer</link><description>
The US FDA on Wednesday approved Revolution Medicines' Rasonque for advanced pancreatic cancer, opening a new treatment option for patients with metastatic disease. A large trial found the once-daily pill doubled survival rates, offering fresh hope for people who have exhausted other treatments.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/664edb68-a19a-11f1-b828-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26238705740891.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/664edb68-a19a-11f1-b828-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26238705740891.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2186cbfe-a1a3-11f1-bf97-e54b5fd5e54a</guid><pubDate>Wed, 26 Aug 2026 23:09:02 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/664edb68-a19a-11f1-b828-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26238705740891.jpg">© Revolution Medicines via AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>‘Shockwaves throughout the country’ following ‘gruesome’ killings in Haitian mountain retreat</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/shockwaves-throughout-the-country-following-gruesome-killings-in-haitian-mountain-retreat</link><description>
Genie Godula is pleased to welcome journalist Harold Isaac on the ground in Haiti's capital, Port-au-Prince. He says what we are witnessing in Haiti is not simply another episode of gang violence, but a profound challenge to the authority of the state at a moment when the country is attempting to return to electoral politics. With armed groups controlling roughly 80 percent of Port-au-Prince, the capital is effectively under siege, while the circulation of people, goods and services increasingly requires some form of negotiation with gang power. The attack in Kenscoff is especially significant because of its proximity to some of the country’s most affluent areas. This as authorities seek to organize Haiti’s first elections in a decade, against a backdrop of arms smuggling, institutional fragility and an unresolved political transition.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/558c2470-a163-11f1-a814-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260826-131020-131546-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/558c2470-a163-11f1-a814-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260826-131020-131546-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5a5ce250-a163-11f1-93b2-a98f70fe4c4f</guid><pubDate>Wed, 26 Aug 2026 15:45:21 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Meta reaches $17 billion settlement with US states over social media harm to teens</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260826-meta-reaches-17-billion-settlement-with-us-states-over-social-media-harm-teens</link><description>
Meta Platforms on Wednesday agreed to pay $17 billion to settle claims, filed by 47 US states, that the company designed Facebook and Instagram to deliberately make teens addicted to their products while deceiving the public, according to state attorneys general. The company agreed to add child-safety measures as part of the settlement. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/31978274-a156-11f1-b2a9-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26230657497731.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/31978274-a156-11f1-b2a9-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26230657497731.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a1f63aba-a156-11f1-81b8-f3a3e4ab8424</guid><pubDate>Wed, 26 Aug 2026 14:31:06 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/31978274-a156-11f1-b2a9-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26230657497731.jpg">© Noah Berger, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Panama and El Salvador declare emergency over El Nino-fuelled drought</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260826-panama-and-el-salvador-declare-emergency-over-el-nino-fuelled-drought</link><description>
Panama and El Salvador have become the latest countries along with Honduras to declare an emergency over El Nino, which has already forced a reduction in shipping through the Panama Canal. All three countries broke their monthly temperature records in both June and July, exacerbating famine concerns.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/242bdd3e-a146-11f1-8801-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6HE99F.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/242bdd3e-a146-11f1-8801-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6HE99F.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5ac4ad4a-a145-11f1-a632-6d1d29b366f3</guid><pubDate>Wed, 26 Aug 2026 12:37:01 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/242bdd3e-a146-11f1-8801-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6HE99F.jpg">© Martin Bernetti, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US country music legend Dolly Parton dies, aged 80</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260826-us-country-music-legend-dolly-parton-dies-aged-80</link><description>
Dolly Parton was one of the rare celebrities that transcended divides in the United States. The country music legend and actress died, aged 80, on August 25.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f3fd0a06-a141-11f1-bb24-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Dolly-Parton.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f3fd0a06-a141-11f1-bb24-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Dolly-Parton.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fc583d10-a141-11f1-ba4a-93d224f347ca</guid><pubDate>Wed, 26 Aug 2026 11:40:15 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Trump scores much-needed double primary victory in South Carolina, Oklahoma</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260826-trump-scores-much-needed-double-primary-victory-in-south-carolina-oklahoma</link><description>
US President Donald Trump scored two badly needed victories Tuesday as his preferred candidates in South Carolina and Oklahoma won the Republican runoffs. The sweep interrupts a bruising run for Trump, whose endorsed candidates had lost 10 Republican contests this cycle, including six in the previous two weeks, as his own approval ratings fell sharply.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/db34251e-a118-11f1-b2b9-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26234036426142.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/db34251e-a118-11f1-b2b9-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26234036426142.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f84e52c6-a11a-11f1-9008-91b23cce887c</guid><pubDate>Wed, 26 Aug 2026 07:41:24 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/db34251e-a118-11f1-b2b9-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26234036426142.jpg">© Mic Smith, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Trump sends Saudi civil nuclear agreement to Congress for review</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260826-trump-saudi-civil-nuclear-agreement-congress</link><description>
US President Donald Trump has submitted a civilian nuclear cooperation agreement with Saudi Arabia to Congress for review, an administration official said. The classified pact, sent to Capitol Hill on Monday, is aimed at bolstering Riyadh’s nuclear programme but remains contingent on Saudi Arabia normalising relations with Israel.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e0ae104c-a0a8-11f1-bd80-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-24T202227Z-1102145854-RC275NA3BY3Q-RTRMADP-3-USA-TRUMP.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e0ae104c-a0a8-11f1-bd80-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-24T202227Z-1102145854-RC275NA3BY3Q-RTRMADP-3-USA-TRUMP.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e1add6aa-a0fb-11f1-9fae-6b23711f873d</guid><pubDate>Wed, 26 Aug 2026 03:17:31 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e0ae104c-a0a8-11f1-bd80-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-24T202227Z-1102145854-RC275NA3BY3Q-RTRMADP-3-USA-TRUMP.jpg">© Jonathan Ernst, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>SpaceX to build $100 billion rocket launch facility in southern Louisiana</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260826-spacex-to-build-100-billion-rocket-launch-complex-in-southern-louisiana</link><description>
SpaceX unveiled plans on Tuesday for a $100 billion rocket launch complex in southern Louisiana, its largest yet, aimed at supporting Starship and AI satellite missions. The 125,000-acre Starbase Louisiana site on Pecan Island could eventually handle thousands of Starship launches annually, the company said.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bc00f5c2-9048-11f1-a14b-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/fc1910c34fb11490f26a136760c8f8e214dd2bd2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bc00f5c2-9048-11f1-a14b-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/fc1910c34fb11490f26a136760c8f8e214dd2bd2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6901bcba-a0f3-11f1-aabc-337eb8d7815a</guid><pubDate>Wed, 26 Aug 2026 02:36:40 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bc00f5c2-9048-11f1-a14b-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/fc1910c34fb11490f26a136760c8f8e214dd2bd2.jpg">© Patrick T. Fallon, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
